		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Aordee - virtual robot design and simulation]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=22189#p22189"><![CDATA[
Hi!<br><br>I've just released a 1.0 version of Aordee, a software for fast and easy creation of robots and mechanisms. With Aordee, you can assemble a robot from a set of components and create an algorithm for moving it using a diagram-based programming language. <br><br>Aordee uses an unmodified version of Bullet Physics. Physics engine works really great, thanks to the creators of BulletPhysics! You can download the software, and check the 'hexapod' sample for a demo of 6-legged robot with 12 engines - it's a fun!<br><br>Please, visit us at <a href="http://www.tensorica.com" class="postlink">http://www.tensorica.com</a><br><br><img src="http://tensorica.com/images/aordee_scr1.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6873">darus</a> — Sun Feb 20, 2011 8:10 pm</p><hr />
